<title>USA: Phoenix Network acquires AmeriConnect.</title>
<headline>Phoenix Network acquires AmeriConnect.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phoenix Network Inc said Wednesday it had acquired AmeriConnect Inc, a Kansas-based reseller of long-distance services, in a stock swap.</p>
<p>Phoenix Network said it expects the deal to increase its annual revenues by more than $17 million, or 19 percent, and add about 6,500 customers to its customer base.</p>
<p>Phoenix said it will issue about 2.6 million common shares in exchange for all shares of capital stock held by AmeriConnect stockholders.</p>
<p>Each share of AmeriConnect is exchangeable for about 0.3605 share of Phoenix common, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
